y8"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:21px;">Are board meetings optional for private limited companies?</span></a></p><p class="text-build-content" style="line-height: 22px; margin: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 10px;" data-testid="EXkH098UZ6voyPgkOUy3q"><span style="color:#767676;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">A board meeting is the coming together of a companyâ€™s board of directors. As the director of a private limited company, the idea of arranging and attending board meetings may seem like an unwanted distraction.</span><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/21/SCF9a_Gp8BdAITvZ3HMi1g/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL3N0YXJ0aW5nLXZpZGVvLXByb2R1Y3Rpb24tY29tcGFueS8"><span style="color:#31a5cb;font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;"> </span></a><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/22/PSoQysVy6a-S0nzZMZIDwQ/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL2FyZS1ib2FyZC1tZWV0aW5ncy1vcHRpb25hbC1mb3ItcHJpdmF0ZS1saW1pdGVkLWNvbXBhbmllcy8"><span style="color:#31a5cb;font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;"><u>Read More</u></span></a></p></div></td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:0px;word-break:break-word;"><div style="height:10px;line-height:10px;">â€Š</div></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="font-size:0px;padding:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;word-break:break-word;"><div style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:21px;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:1;text-align:left;color:#000000;"><p class="text-build-content" data-testid="okbRGatOc1" style="margin: 10px 0; margin-top: 10px;"><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/23/zfdfpKWQhwxsfB_g6Yc65g/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL3Byb3ZpZGUtc2ljay1wYXktdG8tZW1wbG95ZWVzLw"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:21px;line-height:22px;">Do I have to provide sick pay to employees?</span></a></p><p class="text-build-content" style="line-height: 22px; margin: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 10px;" data-testid="okbRGatOc1"><span style="color:#767676;font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;">If you are a UK employer, you have a legal obligation to provide Statutory Sick Pay to all employees and certain groups or workers who meet the required eligibility criteria. Some people may be entitled to more than SSP, depending on their employment contract or your companyâ€™s sickness policy. </span><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/24/CEZII2VlZz9yKYqcWP9CtQ/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL3Byb3ZpZGUtc2ljay1wYXktdG8tZW1wbG95ZWVzLw"><span style="color:#31a5cb;font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;"><u>Read More</u></span></a></p></div></td></tr><tr><td style="font-size:0px;word-break:break-word;"><div style="height:10px;line-height:10px;">â€Š</div></td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="font-size:0px;padding:0px 0px 0px 0px;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;word-break:break-word;"><div style="font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:21px;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:1;text-align:left;color:#000000;"><p class="text-build-content" style="line-height: 22px; margin: 10px 0; margin-top: 10px;" data-testid="ZZAbz5TeDE3xiF4yUVzxK"><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/25/nuj7dxpHiHfRN2gftwdhkw/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL2Nsb3NlLWEtbGltaXRlZC1jb21wYW55LXdpdGgtZGVidHMv"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:Arial;font-size:21px;">How to close a limited company with debts</span></a></p><p class="text-build-content" style="line-height: 22px; margin: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 10px;" data-testid="ZZAbz5TeDE3xiF4yUVzxK"><span style="color:#767676;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;font-size:15px;">If your company cannot afford to pay its bills, it is insolvent. Depending on your particular situation, you can close a limited company with debts by putting it into administration, arranging a creditors' voluntary liquidation, or making an application to the court for compulsory liquidation. </span><a class="link-build-content" style="color:inherit;; text-decoration: none;" target="_blank" href="https://037lq.mjt.lu/lnk/AUYAACAVGP8AAAAFOugAAA10fpoAAAAAd9cAAT3eABzJbgBkwpp8F_hGwPM3QbyheTSOrwzNmAAbd4o/26/4jbFPKcTvFMBlvIK7gIssA/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuMXN0Zm9ybWF0aW9ucy5jby51ay9ibG9nL2Nsb3NlLWEtbGltaXRlZC1jb21wYW55LXdpdGgtZGVidHMv"><span style="color:#31a5cb;font-family:Arial;font-size:15px;"><u>Read More</u></span></a></p></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div><!--[if mso | IE]></td></tr></table><![endif]--></td></tr></tbody></table></div><!--[if mso | IE]></td></tr></table><table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="" role="presentation" style="width:600px;" width="600" ><tr><td style="line-height:0px;font-size:0px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;"><![endif]--><div style="margin:0px auto;max-width:600px;"><table align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="width:100%;"><tbody><tr><td style="direction:ltr;font-size:0px;padding:5px 0px 5px 0px;padding-bottom:5px;padding-left:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-top:5px;text-align:center;"><!--[if mso | IE]><table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td class="" style="v